DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These interfaces may be used to look up information from the
     audit_event(5) database, which describes audit events.  Entries in the
     database are described by _s_t_r_u_c_t _a_u___e_v_e_n_t___e_n_t entries, which are returned
     by calls to ggeettaauueevveenntt(), ggeettaauueevvnnaamm(), or ggeettaauueevvnnuumm().  It is also pos‐
     sible to look up an event number via a call to ggeettaauueevvnnoonnaamm().

     The sseettaauueevveenntt() function resets the database access session for
     audit_event(5), so that the next call to ggeettaauueevveenntt() will start with the
     first entry in the database.

     The eennddaauueevveenntt() function closes the audit_event(5) database session.

     The ggeettaauueevveenntt() function returns a reference to the next entry in the
     audit_event(5) database.

     The ggeettaauueevvnnaamm() function returns a reference to the entry in the
     audit_event(5) database with a name of _n_a_m_e.

     ggeettaauueevvnnuumm() returns a reference to the entry in the audit_event(5) data‐
     base with an event number of _e_v_e_n_t___n_u_m_b_e_r.

     The ggeettaauueevvnnoonnaamm() function returns a reference to an audit event number
     using the audit_event(5) database.

